1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,420
Tired of your quiet routine?
厌倦了平静的日常生活？

2
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:07,840
How about leaving your computer games behind and taking up an extreme sport?
何不放下电脑游戏，开始一项极限运动呢？

3
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:10,180
You can ride a bicycle, right?
你会骑自行车，对吧？

4
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:13,760
In that case you're halfway to becoming a mountain biker.
那样的话，你已经离成为一名山地自行车手不远了。

5
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:19,050
All you have to do is take your bike off the road and try some rough terrain.
你所要做的就是将自行车骑离公路，尝试一些崎岖地形。

6
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:26,500
Mountain biking was developed in California in the 1970s and became an Olympic sport in 1996.
山地自行车运动于20世纪70年代在加利福尼亚发展起来，并于1996年成为奥运会项目。

7
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:34,320
In the London 2012 games athletes had to navigate a 4.7-kilometre track in less than two hours.
在2012年伦敦奥运会上，运动员们必须在不到两小时内完成4.7公里的赛道。

8
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:36,870
Not challenging enough?
还不够有挑战性？

9
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:42,410
Skydivers jump from aircraft at an altitude of 1,000 to 4,000 metres.
跳伞者从1000到4000米高空的飞机上跳下。

10
00:00:42,410 --> 00:00:46,540
You have to be fit but there's no age limit with this sport.
你必须身体健康，但这项运动没有年龄限制。

11
00:00:46,540 --> 00:00:50,750
Dilys Price from Cardiff went on her first jump aged 54.
来自卡迪夫的迪莉丝·普莱斯（Dilys Price）在54岁时尝试了她的第一次跳伞。

12
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:53,850
The minute she came down she wanted to go up again.
她一落地就想再跳一次。

13
00:00:53,850 --> 00:00:56,410
"I was hooked", said Dilys.
“我上瘾了，”迪莉丝说。

14
00:00:56,410 --> 00:01:06,980
Some adrenaline junkies are even bolder – they've invented base jumping, in which people leap from tall structures, such as buildings or bridges, with a parachute.
一些肾上腺素瘾君子甚至更大胆——他们发明了低空跳伞（base jumping），即人们使用降落伞从建筑物或桥梁等高耸结构上跳下。

15
00:01:06,980 --> 00:01:11,250
Many of their stunts aren't legal, especially in urban areas.
他们的许多特技并不合法，尤其是在城市地区。

16
00:01:11,250 --> 00:01:18,210
Dan Witchalls has jumped off The Shard - London's 310 metre-high skyscraper - four times.
丹·威查尔斯（Dan Witchalls）曾四次从伦敦310米高的摩天大楼“碎片大厦”跳下。

17
00:01:18,210 --> 00:01:22,140
He says: "Base jumping is scarier than jumping out of a plane.
他说：“低空跳伞比从飞机上跳伞更可怕。

18
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:30,860
In a plane there's no perception of height, but when you are standing on the edge of the building you can see people and cars - it makes it very real."
在飞机上，你感觉不到高度，但当你站在建筑物的边缘时，你可以看到人和车——这使得这项运动非常真实。”

19
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:37,430
It seems there's no lack of imagination when it comes to risking life to look cool and get the heart pounding.
在冒着生命危险让自己看起来很酷并让心跳加速方面，似乎从不缺乏想象力。

20
00:01:37,430 --> 00:01:40,450
Surfing, scuba diving, rock climbing…
冲浪、潜水、攀岩……

21
00:01:40,450 --> 00:01:44,720
How about turning one of your chores into a daredevil pursuit?
何不将你的一项家务变成一项大胆的消遣？

22
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:48,070
'Extreme ironing' isn't for wimps!
“极限熨烫”可不是懦夫的游戏！

23
00:01:48,070 --> 00:01:52,850
Pressing your shirt on top of a mountain could be dangerous, depending on the mountain.
在山顶上熨烫衬衫可能会很危险，这取决于山的高度。

24
00:01:52,850 --> 00:02:02,820
Extreme ironing is said to have been created in the 1990s in the English town of Leicester by a man who saw a pile of wrinkled clothes and felt bored.
据说，极限熨烫是20世纪90年代由英格兰莱斯特镇的一名男子发明的，他当时看到一堆皱巴巴的衣服感到非常无聊。

25
00:02:02,820 --> 00:02:10,980
That was Phil Shaw who also won the only Extreme Ironing Championships ever held, in Germany in 2002.
这个人就是菲尔·肖（Phil Shaw），他还在2002年德国举办的迄今为止唯一一届极限熨烫锦标赛中获胜。

26
00:02:10,980 --> 00:02:15,970
For him, the thrill of this sport comes from looking at the spectators' faces.
对他来说，这项运动的刺激来自于观察观众的表情。

27
00:02:15,970 --> 00:02:20,640
Shaw says: "Sometimes they look confused, sometimes they laugh.
肖说：“有时他们看起来很困惑，有时他们会笑。

28
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:23,500
It's fun to see how people respond to it."
看到人们的反应很有趣。”
